# Bookmarks file

Target file: `research/bookmarks.md`

## When to apply

Use this rule only when adding, editing, or organizing links in that file.
Do not load or invent bookmark work unless the user provides links or asks for it.

## Format

- Persist content in **English** (titles and any notes)
- One link per bullet: `- [Short title](https://example.com)` — optional trailing note after an em dash
- Keep sections; add a new `## Section` only when none of the existing ones fit
- Default sections: `Official / test info`, `Practice`, `Hiring process`
- Place each link in the best-fitting section; ask only if placement is ambiguous
- Remove placeholder bullets (`- ...`) in a section once it has real links
- Do not duplicate an existing URL; if the title is better, update the existing line
- Keep the file short and scannable — no fluff, no long descriptions

## Placement guide

| Section | Use for |
|---------|---------|
| Official / test info | Criteria/CCAT docs, format, scoring, official vendor pages |
| Practice | Drills, mocks, sample questions, timed practice tools |
| Hiring process | Role, company, application portal, process-specific links |
